{%- comment -%}
  Editorial image-and-text: material/craftsmanship storytelling, or an official-artwork story
  (House Seal / full-body Oryx) when media_source is set to one of those. Material truth, no
  superlatives, no invented facts.

  House Seal / Oryx modes always have real approved artwork to show — a merchant upload, or else
  the bundled official CAVIERA asset (see snippets/caviera-house-seal.liquid and
  snippets/caviera-oryx.liquid) — so this section no longer needs an asset-presence guard for
  those modes. The heading/body copy beside the mark already names it (e.g. "The House Seal"), so
  the mark itself renders decoratively (alt="") to avoid announcing the same thing twice.

  IDENTITY-CORRECTION FIX (Maker's Mark): media_source was already correctly set to "house_seal"
  for the homepage instance — the reported "large Living Oryx" was actually the House Seal, forced
  into an `object-fit: cover; aspect-ratio: 4/5;` box (see .caviera-editorial__media img in
  caviera-home.css) meant for full-bleed photography, not a small formal emblem — cropping/blowing
  it up into something that read as a dominant graphic rather than a refined hallmark. data-media-
  source="{{ media_source }}" below lets caviera-home.css correct ONLY the house_seal case (a
  contained, deliberately modest size) without touching the oryx case at all — the dedicated Oryx
  editorial moment (media_source: "oryx") keeps its exact current appearance, untouched.

  ANIMATION VISIBILITY FIX (Maker's Mark): the previous motion here was a single, one-shot
  IntersectionObserver reveal (assets/caviera-global.js — threshold 0.15, unobserves after firing
  once), the same generic mechanism used for ordinary text blocks across the theme. It fired once,
  briefly, near entry and then did nothing for the remaining ~30svh of scroll through the section —
  there was no continuous scroll-progress driver here at all, unlike Material Truth or Object in
  Focus. That is the confirmed root cause of "feels static": the reveal was real but too brief and
  too early to read as scroll-linked motion.

  scroll_progression (opt-in, default off, exactly like Material Truth's own setting on a different
  section) replaces that one-shot reveal with a dedicated continuous system — see
  assets/caviera-makers-mark.js, which writes three independent, overlapping 0–1 progress channels
  (--maker-seal-progress, --maker-headline-progress, --maker-provenance-progress) as the user
  actually scrolls through the section, plus a lightweight entry-based (non-scroll-linked) mobile
  mode. Off by default — this section is reused for the calmer, static Oryx moment, which keeps its
  exact current one-shot behaviour untouched; only the homepage's "makers-mark" instance turns this
  on (templates/index.json). When scroll_progression is on, the older per-element media_motion /
  heading_motion reveal attributes are intentionally omitted below so the two systems never both
  apply to the same element at once.

  Provenance block (opt-in, default off) — a small, neutral "Edition Record" line, never a
  fabricated production count (no "017/100"-style denominator unless a real Edition quantity is
  ever confirmed).

  ORYX THRESHOLD CROSSING (opt-in, default off, and further guarded to media_source == 'oryx' only
  — it can never accidentally engage on the Maker's Mark/House Seal instance even if the setting
  were toggled on there by mistake). A second, independent continuous scroll system alongside
  scroll_progression above — deliberately NOT sharing its --maker-*-progress channels or its
  .caviera-editorial__stage[data-caviera-editorial-progress] wrapper attribute, per this project's
  own rule that every section keeps its own independently-named progress variable. See assets/
  caviera-oryx-crossing.js: one continuous 0-1 progress value drives the Oryx artwork through three
  authored keyframes (arrival → crossing → composure) as --oryx-x/--oryx-y/--oryx-scale/--oryx-
  opacity, and two narrower windows of that same progress drive the label/heading and body copy at
  their own, calmer deltas. The artwork itself is never redrawn, replaced or cropped — only moved
  and faded as one object via transform/opacity.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign media_source = section.settings.media_source | default: 'custom_image'
  assign seal_mode = 'light'
  unless section.settings.color_scheme == 'bone'
    assign seal_mode = 'dark'
  endunless
  assign use_progress = section.settings.scroll_progression
  assign use_oryx_crossing = false
  if section.settings.oryx_crossing_motion and media_source == 'oryx'
    assign use_oryx_crossing = true
  endif
-%}
<section class="caviera-section caviera-editorial" data-scheme="{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}" data-reverse="{{ section.settings.image_position }}">
  {%- comment -%}
    Stage/stage-inner only exists when scroll_progression or oryx_crossing_motion is on (same
    wrapper pattern used by Material Truth: an in-flow ancestor with an explicit height, a sticky
    inner that pins for that height, giving the matching JS a real scroll distance to compute
    continuous progress from). Every other instance of this section renders the grid directly,
    byte-for-byte as before. The two features carry distinct attributes so they never collide.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if use_progress or use_oryx_crossing -%}<div class="caviera-editorial__stage"{% if use_progress %} data-caviera-editorial-progress{% endif %}{% if use_oryx_crossing %} data-caviera-oryx-progress{% endif %}>
  <div class="caviera-editorial__stage-inner">{%- endif -%}
  <div class="container--full caviera-editorial__grid">
    <div class="caviera-editorial__media" data-media-source="{{ media_source }}"{% if section.settings.media_motion and use_progress == false and use_oryx_crossing == false %} data-reveal data-reveal-style="seal-resolve"{% endif %}>
      {%- if use_progress and media_source == 'house_seal' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Optional Bureau Nine depth cue: one faint, always-static-opacity impression of the same
          approved Seal sitting behind the real one — never a second visible mark, never sharp.
          Hidden on mobile (kept lightweight there, per brief). If this ever reads as busy/decorative
          rather than quietly spatial, delete this single block; nothing else depends on it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="caviera-editorial__media-impression" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: seal_mode, width: 280, alt: '' -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- case media_source -%}
        {%- when 'house_seal' -%}
          {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: seal_mode, width: 280, alt: '' -%}
        {%- when 'oryx' -%}
          {%- render 'caviera-oryx', variant: 'static', mode: seal_mode, width: 320, alt: '' -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if section.settings.image -%}
            <img
              src="{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
              srcset="{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w, {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w"
              sizes="(min-width: 900px) 50vw, 100vw"
              width="{{ section.settings.image.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.image.height }}"
              alt="{{ section.settings.image.alt | default: '' | escape }}"
              loading="lazy"
            >
          {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
            <div class="caviera-editor-note">Add an image.</div>
          {%- endif -%}
      {%- endcase -%}
    </div>
    <div class="caviera-editorial__text"{% unless use_progress or use_oryx_crossing %} data-reveal{% endunless %}>
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Drkst-style typographic moment, opt-in per instance (see heading_motion below) — off by
          default since this same section also renders the calmer, ceremonial Oryx moment; only used
          when neither continuous system (scroll_progression / oryx_crossing_motion) is on, since
          each of those drives the heading itself instead.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h2 class="heading-h2"{% if section.settings.heading_motion and use_progress == false and use_oryx_crossing == false %} data-reveal data-reveal-style="drkst"{% endif %}>{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}<div class="body-text">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.link_text != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.link_url }}" class="link-underline">{{ section.settings.link_text }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_provenance -%}
        <div class="caviera-editorial__provenance">
          {%- if section.settings.provenance_label != blank -%}<span class="caviera-editorial__provenance-label label">{{ section.settings.provenance_label }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.provenance_line != blank -%}<p class="caviera-editorial__provenance-line">{{ section.settings.provenance_line }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          <span class="caviera-editorial__provenance-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {%- if section.settings.provenance_mark != blank -%}<span class="caviera-editorial__provenance-mark label">{{ section.settings.provenance_mark }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- if use_progress or use_oryx_crossing -%}</div>
</div>{%- endif -%}
</section>

<script src="{{ 'caviera-makers-mark.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'caviera-oryx-crossing.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Editorial media & text",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "media_source", "label": "Media source", "default": "custom_image",
      "options": [
        { "value": "custom_image", "label": "Custom image" },
        { "value": "house_seal", "label": "Official House Seal" },
        { "value": "oryx", "label": "Official full-body Oryx" }
      ],
      "info": "House Seal / Oryx modes use the bundled official CAVIERA artwork automatically; upload your own under Theme settings → CAVIERA Identity only to override it."
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Colour", "default": "bone",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bone", "label": "Warm Bone" },
        { "value": "cinnabar", "label": "Cinnabar" },
        { "value": "obsidian", "label": "Obsidian" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "image_position", "label": "Image position", "default": "left",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "Right" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image", "info": "Used only when media source is Custom image." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Material & craft" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Precision, by hand." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "heading_motion", "label": "Oversized heading entrance", "default": false, "info": "A restrained Drkst-style typographic moment for this heading. Ignored when scroll progression (below) is on. Off by default — this section is reused for the calmer, ceremonial Oryx moment." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "media_motion", "label": "Quiet resolve-on-scroll for the mark", "default": false, "info": "A restrained opacity/position settle as the mark enters view. Ignored when scroll progression (below) is on. Off by default." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "scroll_progression", "label": "Continuous scroll-linked reveal", "default": false, "info": "Replaces the entrance reveals above with a slow, formal, continuously scroll-linked sequence for the mark, heading and Edition record. Off by default; the homepage's Maker's Mark instance turns it on explicitly." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "oryx_crossing_motion", "label": "Oryx threshold crossing (scroll-linked)", "default": false, "info": "Moves the Oryx artwork itself — never redrawn — through the space as the section is read. Only ever applies when Media source above is the official full-body Oryx; off by default." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_text", "label": "Link text" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link_url", "label": "Link URL" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_provenance", "label": "Show Edition record", "default": false, "info": "A small, neutral provenance line beneath the copy. Off by default." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "provenance_label", "label": "Provenance label", "default": "Edition Record" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "provenance_line", "label": "Provenance line", "default": "CAVIERA No. ______" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "provenance_mark", "label": "Provenance mark", "default": "House Seal / Authenticated" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Editorial media & text" }]
}
{% endschema %}
